    "ls|LS17_S9_U_215": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION    \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION  \n \nLOK SABHA  \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 215 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2022 \n \nCentral University in Rajasthan \n \n†215. SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH JOSHI: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to establish a Central University in Rajasthan; \n(b) if so, whether the Government has received any proposal from the Government of \nRajasthan; \n(c) if so, the details thereof; \n(d) whether the Government proposes to conduct an Entrance Test at national level for \nadmission in all the Central Universities of the country; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof;  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(DR. SUBHAS SARKAR ) \n \n(a) to  (e) Setting up of a Central University is a continuous  process. There is already a \nCentral University in the State of Rajasthan namely the Central University of Rajasthan. \nHowever, at present there is no proposal under consideration in the Ministry for setting up of \na new Central University in Rajasthan.  \n \nIn pursuance of the National Education Policy, 2020, it has been decided to conduct \ncommon entrance test for admission  in central universities from the academic year 2022 -23 \nto reduce the burden on students, universities and the entire education system.  The Common \nUniversity Entrance Test ( CUET) for undergraduate programme is to  assess the students of \ndifferent boards at the same level, giving them equal opportunity . It is convenient for \nstudents as they can  apply to more than one universities as per their choice with  one \napplication form. They can appear in the test in 13 languages over hundreds of examination \ncentres. The syllabus for undergraduate level is based on the understanding of subject at \nclass XII level, irrespective of affiliations to any board.  \n \n***** ",
