    "ls|LS17_S9_U_26": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.26 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.07.2022 \n  \nDEVELOPMENT OF CAVES IN BORIVALI NATIONAL PARK. \n \n†26. SHRI GOPAL CHINNAYA SHETTY: \nWill the Minister of Culture be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the location-wise details of rare Souvenirs/Monuments/Idols/Caves of Hindu deities \nbelonging to ancient period in the country especially in Maharashtra; \n(b) whether the Government has taken any step or proposes to take steps for formulating \nnew rules as per t he present requirement to develop, preserve and beautify the rare \nSouvenirs/Monuments/Idols/Caves of Hindu deities belonging to ancient period in the \ncountry especially in Mandapeshwar Caves situated in Boriwali and Dahisar in \nMumbai North Parliamentary Co nstituency and Kanheri caves in Boriwali National \nPark and also for immediately repealing rules formulated during British era in this \nregard;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof; \n(d) whether the Government has received request from the representatives of people in \nMay, 2022 in this regard; \n(e) if so, the details thereof; and \n(f) the action taken or proposed to be taken by the Government in this   regard? \n   \nANSWER \n \n                                    THE MINISTER OF CULTURE, TOURISM AND \n                                    DEVELOPMENT OF NORTH EASTERN REGION \n \n                                                    (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n (a) Location-wise details of monuments and sites of National importance in the country \nincluding Maharashtra are available on website of Archaeological Survey of India,  \n<https://asi.nic.in>  \n(b) \n&  \n(c) \nAll ancient mo numents and archaeological sites declared as of national importance \nincluding idols and caves are duly conserved, preserved and maintained under the \nprovisions of Ancient Monuments and Archaeological Sites and Remains Act 1958  \nand Rules 1959 made thereunder.  \n(d) \nto  \n(f) \nNo such representation was received regarding change in rules. However, a letter \nwas received in May,2022 requesting installation of a modern statue in Kanheri \nCaves which was replied.  \n***** ",
